{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"89e86a96af6947632cca8aae8330b89858f13bbbdc5af8227ea1b045fcc6b2f8","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge scheduling and CloudWatch monitoring","key_entities":["reconcile-bridge.yml","RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS","23 * * * *","bridge_run_failures","monitoring_bridge.tf","canary_bridge.py","docs/jira-sync-setup.md","Jenkinsfile","terraform-drift.yml"],"problem_keywords":["bridge schedule","continuous reconciliation","cron","hourly cadence","monitoring alarm"],"propositions":["The bridge must change from continuous self-dispatch to hourly schedule via single cron entry '23 * * * *' in reconcile-bridge.yml, replacing the three-entry 40-minute workaround.","The CloudWatch bridge_run_failures alarm becomes structurally unfirable at hourly cadence (max one pass per 3600s bucket) and must be retuned to threshold=0, evaluation_periods=2, datapoints_to_alarm=2 to preserve failure detection.","All cadence references (40 minutes) must be updated to hourly across workflows, tests, documentation, and comments to prevent silent monitoring regression and adoption confusion.","A terraform apply is required to deploy the alarm change; terraform-drift will remain red until applied, and the deployed alarm will be outdated until then."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786656840998324001,"uuid":"27570e51-2253-4fd9-a728-b6fb58daa985"}